pokeheartgold-route.patch (tools/pokehg_gen.py applies the patches in name order: before widepointers2, which also changes ov12_0225E250's file): the
route pilot's hooks for HeartGold and SoulSilver (tools/route.py hg / ss, docs/hgss.md "Route tool"), as
pokeplatinum-route.patch's for Platinum. Calls into port/game/route_gen4.c (its HEARTGOLD half). Test-only: the pilot does
nothing unless its environment variables are set; game behaviour and the DS build are unchanged (the calls are the port's).
- field_system.c FieldSystem_Main: PortRoute4_Frame once per field frame, after the frame's field task and processes (the
  pilot's PortRouteState: zone, tile, event; the map adapter).
- start_menu.c (the touch-screen field menu): Task_StartMenu_HandleInput calls PortRoute4_StartMenu each frame it reads keys
  (gPortRouteMenu: input, cursor, SAVE, the key toward SAVE); SAVE chosen (Task_StartMenu_HandleSelection_Save) calls
  PortRoute4_SaveStart, the menu back from the save app (sub_0203D288) PortRoute4_SaveEnd.
- touch_save_app.c: PortRoute4_Saved after Field_SaveGameNormal (the write).
- scrcmd_c.c sub_020416E4 (ScrCmd_YesNo's wait): PortRoute4_YesNo with the cursor's row each frame, -1 at the answer (Py, Pn).
- overlay 1's field menu tasks (ov01_021EDE8C: ScrCmd_MenuExec's 2D menu; ov01_021EE49C: the scrolling list): PortRoute4_FieldMenu
  each frame they read keys and at the answer (Pl:N).
- the battle pilot (overlay 12, the player's tasks): ov12_0225DAD4 (the action menu), ov12_0225E250 (the move menu; its
  local struct gets MoveSelectMenuData's invalidMoves) and ov12_0225FA44 (the yes/no) call PortRoute4_BattleMenu each frame
  they wait, ov12_022609F8 (forget a move) too; the move menu's answer goes through PortRoute4_BattleMove.
- the test cheats: battle_controller_player.c ov12_0224B1FC (PP) and BattleSystem_CheckMoveHit ask PortRoute4_CheatSide,
  BattleControllerPlayer_HpCalc PortRoute4_CheatDamage; battle_command.c BtlCmd_UpdateHealthbar and
  BtlCmd_UpdateHealthbarValue pass hpCalc through PortRoute4_CheatHpCalc (the player's side's HP loss a script applies: burn,
  poison, weather, Leech Seed, Curse, recoil, Spikes); overlay_12_0224E4FC.c CheckSortSpeed PortRoute4_CheatSpeed;
  field/field_control.c FieldSystem_CheckWildEncounter PortRoute4_NoEncounter.
- script_manager.c SetupScriptEngine (every script start: StartMapSceneScript, QueueScript, StartScriptFromMenu): PortRoute4_ScriptStart(script)
  (the interaction sweep's log of the script ids a talk, a sign or a trigger tile began: tools/hg_int_sweep.py).
- the party "knows" the field moves under the test cheat (BWPORT_TESTCHEAT=win; the badge checks stay real, port/game/route_gen4.c
  PortRoute4_CheatFieldMove): scrcmd_party.c ScrCmd_GetPartySlotWithMove (the std scripts of Cut, Rock Smash, Strength, Rock Climb, Surf,
  Waterfall, Whirlpool) answers slot 0, script_pokemon_util.c GetIdxOfFirstPartyMonWithMove (the field's Surf and Waterfall checks,
  field_control.c) 0.
- F:fly (port/src/route_fly.h): party_menu.c PortRoute4_PartyMenu each frame the list takes keys (PartyMenu_Subtask_MainNormal) and
  each frame of the context menu (PartyMenu_Subtask_HandleContextMenuInput); the Pokegear's fly map (fly_map.c) PortRoute4_FlyMap each
  frame of FlyMap_MainTask_HandleInput / _ContextMenu, PortRoute4_TownMapEnd at FlyMap_Exit (the pick and its map).
